Single Purpose Description: The single purpose of this extension is to allow users to flip (horizontally/vertically) and rotate (90/180/270 degrees) web pages or specific elements (like videos and images) directly within the browser for better viewing and accessibility.

Context Menus Justification: This permission is required to add "Flip" and "Rotate" options to the right-click context menu, allowing users to quickly transform the specific element or page they are interacting with.

Storage Justification: This permission is used to save user preferences, such as the "Whitelist" of sites where the extension should be automatically enabled, and to persist the state of the interactive panel (e.g., position on screen).

Host Permission Justification: The extension needs access to all hosts (<all_urls>) because its core functionality is to inject a content script that performs CSS transformations (flip/rotate) on ANY website the user visits. Without this, the extension cannot modify the page content as requested by the user.

No data collected from any users. All options unchecked.